module ga-superior-court-civil.civil

start complaint-filed

state complaint-filed: "Complaint filed" by applicant cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 36.10"
{
  note "A complaint or petition is filed only when accompanied by the filing fee, the fee for sheriff service or a pauper's affidavit, a civil case initiation form and any forms required by law or rule; the filer furnishes the service copies (Rule 36.10). Commencement and service of process are governed by the Civil Practice Act (O.C.G.A. §§ 9-11-3, 9-11-4), which is not vendored: the service period is not stated. Periods in this package are stated, not counted: the counting statute (O.C.G.A. § 1-3-1) is not vendored."
  edge-complaint-filed-service "Summons issued and served" -> service {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 36.11"
  }
}

state service: "Service and return of service" by office cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 36.11"
{
  note "The sheriff or other authorized person enters the return of service on a form provided by the clerk and files it with the clerk (Rule 36.11). Dismissal for untimely service is a matter of the Civil Practice Act, which is not vendored, and is not modeled."
  edge-service-answer "Served" -> answer-due { authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 15" }
}

decision answer-due: "Answer, motion or default" by office cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 15"
{
  note "The answer period (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-12(a)) and default (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-55) are not vendored, so the period is not stated. The Uniform Rules start the discovery period 30 days after service when no answer is filed within 30 days of service or by the date set by an extension or order (Rule 5.1); that is a discovery rule, not the answer deadline."
  edge-answer-due-default "No defensive pleading filed" -> default-entered {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 15"
  }
  edge-answer-due-motion "Motion filed" -> pleading-motion {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.1"
  }
  edge-answer-due-answer "Answer filed" -> case-management {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 5.1"
  }
}

decision pleading-motion: "Motion decided" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"
{
  note "A pretrial motion includes citations of supporting authorities and, where unstipulated facts are relied on, affidavits or citations to the record; an e-filer notifies the opposing parties and the assigned judge by e-mail no later than 24 hours after e-filing (Rule 6.1). Unless the judge orders otherwise or law provides, each opposing party serves and files its response not later than 30 days after service of the motion (Rule 6.2). Motions are decided without oral hearing unless the court orders otherwise (Rule 6.3). The grounds of a motion to dismiss and amendment of pleadings are the Civil Practice Act's (O.C.G.A. §§ 9-11-12(b), 9-11-15), not vendored; the re-pleading loop is not modeled. No leading decision is named."
  edge-pleading-motion-dismissed "Granted" -> dismissed-pleading {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"
  }
  edge-pleading-motion-denied "Denied" -> case-management {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"
  }
}

terminal default-entered: "Default judgment" outcome [loss] cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 15"
{
  note "The party seeking a default judgment certifies in writing, attached to the proposed judgment, the date and type of service, that proof of service was filed within 5 business days of service (or the date it was filed), that no defensive pleading has been filed as shown by court records, and the defendant's military status if required (Rule 15). Opening a default is the Civil Practice Act's (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-55(b)), not vendored, and is not modeled. Outcome from the defending side."
}

terminal dismissed-pleading: "Dismissed on the motion" outcome [win, dismissal] cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"

state case-management: "Early planning conference and discovery plan" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 5.4"
{
  note "The parties may agree to, the judge may order, or a party may petition for an early planning discovery conference (Rule 5.4(1)). After it the parties may submit an agreed discovery plan within 14 days of the meeting, or, without agreement, a joint report within 14 days stating each party's position (Rule 5.4(2), (3)). The court may set a pretrial conference sua sponte or on motion (Rule 7.1)."
  edge-case-management-discovery "Discovery begins" -> discovery {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 5.1"
  }
}

state discovery: "Discovery" by applicant cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 5.1"
{
  note "To use the court's compulsory process to compel discovery, discovery must be commenced promptly and completed within 6 months after the filing of the answer, or, when no answer is filed within 30 days of service, within 6 months beginning 30 days after service; the court may open, extend, reopen or shorten that time (Rule 5.1). Original discovery material is not filed except as O.C.G.A. § 9-11-29.1(a) requires, but a certificate of service of written discovery is filed (Rule 5.2). A deposition is limited to one day of seven hours unless authorized or stipulated (Rule 5.3). A motion to compel quotes or attaches each request at issue and is filed with a certificate that counsel conferred in good faith (Rule 6.4)."
  edge-discovery-sj "Summary judgment motion filed" -> sj-motion {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.5"
  }
  edge-discovery-pretrial "No summary judgment motion" -> pretrial {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 7.1"
  }
  edge-discovery-settle "Settled or dismissed" -> settled {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 4.10"
  }
}

decision sj-motion: "Summary judgment decided" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.5"
{
  note "The motion annexes a separate, short and concise statement of each theory of recovery and each material fact as to which the movant contends there is no genuine issue to be tried; the response includes a statement of each material fact as to which a genuine issue is contended to exist (Rule 6.5). The motion is filed early enough not to delay the trial, and no trial is continued by reason of its delayed filing (Rule 6.6). The response is due not later than 30 days after service of the motion unless ordered otherwise (Rule 6.2). The motion is decided without oral hearing unless a separate 'Request for Oral Hearing' is filed with the motion or not later than 5 days after the time for response (Rule 6.3); the time requirements for summary judgment are not shortened as emergency motions (Rule 6.7). The summary judgment standard (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-56) is not vendored. The outline's leading decision, Lau's Corp. v. Haskins, 261 Ga. 491 (1991), is removed: no reporter text of it is vendored."
  edge-sj-motion-granted "Granted" -> judgment-for-movant {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.5"
  }
  edge-sj-motion-denied "Denied or partly denied" -> pretrial {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 7.1"
  }
}

terminal judgment-for-movant: "Judgment for the movant" outcome [win, judgment] cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.5"
{
  note "Partial summary judgment is not modeled."
}

state pretrial: "Pretrial conference and order" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 7.1"
{
  note "When a pretrial conference is ordered, it is attended by the attorneys who will try the action, and each party presents a written proposed pretrial order; failure to appear without legal excuse or to present one authorizes removal from the trial calendar, entry of a pretrial order or another sanction except dismissal with prejudice (Rules 7.1, 7.2)."
  edge-pretrial-trial "Placed on the ready list" -> trial {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 8.2"
  }
  edge-pretrial-settle "Settled or dismissed" -> settled {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 4.10"
  }
}

decision trial: "Trial calendar and trial" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 8.3"
{
  note "An action is placed on the ready list by the assigned judge on notice, or by a party after entry of a pretrial order on notice (Rule 8.2). The trial calendar is distributed or published not less than 20 days before the session at which the listed actions are tried (Rule 8.3); the first 10 actions on it appear ready for trial on the date specified unless directed otherwise (Rule 8.4). Continuances are not granted merely by agreement, and a penalty of up to $50 may be imposed on a party first moving for a continuance within 5 days of the trial week absent statutory grounds or good cause (Rule 8.5). Argument in a civil case other than an appeal from a magistrate court is limited to 2 hours each side (Rule 13.1(D)). A civil action voluntarily dismissed after the jury is empaneled, other than by a settlement dictated into the record, bears all court costs including juror fees (Rule 12)."
  edge-trial-verdict "Verdict or decision" -> post-trial {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"
  }
  edge-trial-no-response "Failure to respond to the call for trial" -> dismissed-no-response {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 14"
  }
}

terminal dismissed-no-response: "Dismissed without prejudice for failure to respond to the call" outcome [loss, dismissal] cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 14"
{
  note "On its own motion or the opposite party's, the court may dismiss without prejudice a civil action, or a party's pleading, on the failure to properly respond to the call of the action for trial or other proceeding (Rule 14). Outcome from the side that failed to respond."
}

decision post-trial: "Post-trial motions decided" by court cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 41.1"
{
  note "Motions for new trial and for judgment notwithstanding the verdict are heard orally, unlike other civil motions (Rule 6.3). The motion for new trial is heard and decided as promptly as possible (Rule 41.1). The periods for these motions (O.C.G.A. §§ 5-5-40, 9-11-50(b)) are not vendored."
  edge-post-trial-judgment "Motions resolved or none filed" -> judgment-entered {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 41.1"
  }
  edge-post-trial-jnov "Judgment notwithstanding the verdict granted" -> judgment-for-movant {
    authority cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 6.3"
  }
}

state judgment-entered: "Judgment filed" by office cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 36.10"
{
  note "Judgments, settlements, dismissals and other dispositions are filed only with a civil case disposition form (Rule 36.10). Entry of judgment under the Civil Practice Act (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-58) is not vendored."
  edge-judgment-entered-appeal "Next step" -> appeal-decision {
    authority cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 16"
  }
}

decision appeal-decision: "Notice of appeal within time?" by applicant cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 16"
{
  note "The notice-of-appeal period (O.C.G.A. § 5-6-38) and appellate jurisdiction are statutes that are not vendored, so the period is not stated. An extension may be sought in the Court of Appeals under O.C.G.A. § 5-6-39 before the period expires, after a bona fide effort to obtain it from the trial court; only one is permitted, and it cannot exceed the time otherwise allowed (Ga. Ct. App. R. 16(a))."
  edge-appeal-decision-taken "Notice filed" -> appeal-taken { authority cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 11" }
  edge-appeal-decision-none "No notice filed" -> final-no-appeal {
    authority cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 16"
  }
}

terminal appeal-taken: "Appeal taken: continue in the Court of Appeals package" outcome [appeal] cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 11"
{
  note "Hand-off to lit/gactapp (ga-court-of-appeals-civil-appeals). The appeal is docketed once the notice of appeal, the record and any requested transcripts are filed in the Clerk's office; one within another court's jurisdiction is transferred by order (Ga. Ct. App. R. 11(a), (b)). On remittitur, the notice of appeal, remittitur and index are filed with the original action (Unif. Super. Ct. R. 38)."
}

terminal final-no-appeal: "Final: no appeal" outcome [final] cite "Ga. Ct. App. R. 16"

terminal settled: "Settled or dismissed" outcome [settlement] cite "Unif. Super. Ct. R. 4.10"
{
  note "Immediately on the settlement or dismissal of a civil action the attorneys notify the assigned judge and, where appropriate, the calendar clerk (Rule 4.10). Voluntary dismissal itself is the Civil Practice Act's (O.C.G.A. § 9-11-41(a)), not vendored."
}
